- Direct local file viewing succeeds in all three engines with JS disabled and no HTTP(S) requests. Chromium/Firefox use offline=True; WebKit uses a normal context with both HTTP and HTTPS blocked, avoiding the previously observed runner offline-emulation error. No compiler or server is needed to view these generated bytes.
- Representative narrow heading/body, narrow S06 list, and wide page screenshots were visually checked. Human screen-reader operation and real Safari device QA were not performed.

